<title>GERMANY: German BW state June CPI up 1.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German BW state June CPI up 1.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The statistics office in the west German state of Baden-Wuerttemberg said on Tuesday that the cost of living rose 0.2 percent in June from May and was up 1.4 percent from June 1996.</p>
<p>In May, the state had reported a month-on-month rise of 0.3 percent and a year-on-year increase of 1.3 percent.</p>
<p>Data for four west German states are used to calculate a preliminary figure for west Germany as a whole.  </p>
<p>The Statistics Office in Baden Wuerttemberg gave the following breakdown of its June cost of living data :</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr  Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     +0.2	1.4    115.7</p>
<p> Prices heating oil			-1.8	+6.8    88.5</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.2	+2.4   125.8</p>
<p> Household energy			  +0.1	+2.5   120.4</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  +1.3	+2.0   125.2</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  unch	+0.1   115.1</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods +0.1	+0.7   112.6</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   +0.5	+1.6   111.9</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   unch	+0.2   110.9</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	unch	+1.1   113.9</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   -0.2	+2.1   114.7</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
